{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778942286,"nonce":"6p/nUX9LSzEyCOqnPmxBI+QGAHs=","message":"## Implementation design v0: operational integration on canonical issue IDs\n\nThis issue moves operational Mandible records onto ledger issue identity while keeping legacy fields long enough for compatibility and rollback.\n\n### Principle\n\nDo not duplicate issue semantics. The ledger owns issue identity, comments, labels, status, relationships, and issue events. Existing operational tables still own their domains:\n\n- `work_units` owns work dispatch/lifecycle.\n- `auth_requests` owns protected-action approval/execution lifecycle.\n- `sessions` / `console_sessions` / `conversations` own agent runtime and transcripts.\n- `issue_resolutions` or its replacement owns commit-to-issue resolution evidence.\n\nThis issue adds canonical joins and events between those domains.\n\n### Work units\n\nA work unit currently has one `issue_id` and `repo_id`. Keep those fields during migration, but add canonical linkage.\n\nRecommended schema:\n\n```sql\nALTER TABLE work_units ADD COLUMN ledger_issue_id TEXT REFERENCES ledger_issues(id);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_work_units_ledger_issue ON work_units(ledger_issue_id);\n```\n\nBecause SQLite `ALTER TABLE` constraints can be limited and legacy rows may precede the ledger, tests should verify the exact migration behavior. If adding an FK directly is too brittle, use a canonical link table instead:\n\n```sql\nledger_work_unit_issue_links (\n  work_unit_id TEXT NOT NULL,\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n  relationship_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'work_unit_tracks',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (work_unit_id, issue_id)\n);\n```\n\nPreferred steady state: work-unit queries join by canonical issue ID, while legacy `issue_id`/`repo_id` remain only for compatibility and old clients.\n\nWork-unit command behavior:\n\n- claim/activate/release/patch should resolve input issue refs through `LedgerStore.resolveIssueRef` when ledger mode is enabled;\n- transitions append ledger events such as `work_unit:claimed`, `work_unit:activated`, `work_unit:committed`, `work_unit:resolved`, `work_unit:abandoned`, `work_unit:assigned`;\n- liveness remains derived at query time, not stored as ledger state;\n- continuation text remains on the work unit, but a continuation-created event can be appended for timeline visibility.\n\n### Sessions\n\nExisting `session_issues(session_id, issue_id, repo_id)` is short-ID based. Keep it for compatibility and add canonical links.\n\nRecommended schema:\n\n```sql\nledger_session_issue_links (\n  session_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES sessions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n  link_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'worked_on',\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'system',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  last_seen_at INTEGER,\n  metadata_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  PRIMARY KEY (session_id, issue_id, link_type)\n);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_ledger_session_issue_issue ON ledger_session_issue_links(issue_id);\n```\n\nLink types, first cut:\n\n- `worked_on`\n- `spawned_for`\n- `mentioned`\n- `auth_origin`\n- `handoff`\n\nSession graph/detail behavior:\n\n- active/idle sessions are live operational overlays;\n- stopped/dead sessions are historical issue records;\n- parent/child session relationships continue to use `sessions.parent_id`, with graph projection deciding collapse/layout;\n- no attempt in this issue to infer every issue mention from full transcripts unless the source is deterministic.\n\n### Auth requests\n\nAuth request issue references currently live in JSON fields and commit messages. Normalize them.\n\nRecommended schema:\n\n```sql\nledger_auth_issue_links (\n  auth_request_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES auth_requests(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n  link_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'resolves',\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'auth_queue',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  metadata_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  PRIMARY KEY (auth_request_id, issue_id, link_type)\n);\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_ledger_auth_issue_issue ON ledger_auth_issue_links(issue_id);\n```\n\nLink types:\n\n- `resolves`\n- `references`\n- `depends_on`\n- `caused_by`\n- `tests`\n\nAuth submission behavior:\n\n- parse explicit `--issue` / `issues` fields and `Bug:` trailers;\n- resolve aliases with project/repo context;\n- store canonical auth links;\n- preserve legacy JSON fields until all consumers migrate;\n- reject or warn on ambiguous issue refs rather than silently selecting one.\n\nAuth completion behavior:\n\n- on successful merge, append ledger events for auth completion and issue resolution;\n- close/resolve linked issues through ledger commands when the auth request is intended to resolve them;\n- enqueue git-bug export through outbox rather than synchronously closing git-bug issues on the hot path;\n- preserve current auth queue status/result behavior.\n\n### Commit and resolution links\n\nBackfill `issue_resolutions` into canonical links/events.\n\nRecommended schema if a new table is useful:\n\n```sql\nledger_commit_issue_links (\n  commit_sha TEXT NOT NULL,\n  repo_project_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_projects(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n  issue_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES ledger_issues(id) ON DELETE RESTRICT,\n  link_type TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'fixed_by',\n  source TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'auth_queue',\n  created_at INTEGER NOT NULL,\n  metadata_json TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT '{}',\n  PRIMARY KEY (commit_sha, issue_id, link_type)\n);\n```\n\nCommit trailers should remain human-friendly during migration, but internal state should store canonical IDs. `Bug: 097d2b7` can stay acceptable when repo/project context resolves it unambiguously.\n\n### Actor convention\n\nUse the same actor vocabulary from the ledger core issue:\n\n- `mandible_user`: direct action inside Mandible UI/CLI by the configured user;\n- `agent`: Claude/Codex/Gemini/etc. with session/console identity where known;\n- `system`: internal automation/reconciler/auth executor;\n- `external_adapter`: git-bug import/export or future adapters.\n\nFor comments created through Mandible UI, use configurable Mandible user display identity. For agent-created comments or auth requests, include session/agent identity if available.\n\n### Backfill strategy\n\nBackfill should be explicit and report coverage:\n\n1. Build an alias resolver map from ledger aliases to canonical issues.\n2. Backfill `work_units.ledger_issue_id` or work-unit link table from legacy `issue_id` + `repo_id`.\n3. Backfill session links from `session_issues`.\n4. Backfill auth links from `auth_requests.issue_ids`, `auth_requests.issues`, and `Bug:` trailers in `commit_message`.\n5. Backfill commit links from `issue_resolutions`.\n6. Emit a report of resolved, unresolved, and ambiguous references by source table.\n\nUnresolved/ambiguous refs should not be dropped. Store them in report/conflict metadata so they can be repaired.\n\n### Route integration points\n\nThe following current behavior needs canonical joins:\n\n- issue context endpoint currently joins work units by `(issue_id, repo_id)`;\n- issue sessions endpoint reads `session_issues`;\n- spawn-from-issue finds work unit/branch/continuation and then updates `assigned_session_id`;\n- work-unit routes claim/activate/release by legacy issue/repo;\n- auth graph code reads `auth_requests.issue_ids` and commit messages.\n\nImplement adapters/mappers so legacy endpoints still work while canonical joins are available.\n\n### Tests\n\nRequired tests:\n\n- work-unit backfill resolves aliases and records unresolved/ambiguous rows;\n- work-unit claim/activate emits ledger events in ledger mode;\n- session link backfill preserves old links and creates canonical rows;\n- auth request issue parsing resolves explicit issue IDs and `Bug:` trailers through project context;\n- auth completion updates ledger issue status/resolution and emits events;\n- commit resolution backfill creates canonical commit-issue links;\n- issue context endpoint can be served from canonical links while preserving existing response shape;\n- spawn-from-issue still finds branch/continuation and assigns sessions;\n- dead/stopped sessions appear as history but do not become live graph actor records.\n\n### Non-goals\n\n- Do not rewrite the auth queue UI here.\n- Do not infer arbitrary issue mentions from full transcripts here.\n- Do not remove legacy fields in this issue.\n- Do not change work-unit liveness from derived to stored state.\n\n### Done check\n\nAfter this issue, operational Mandible records can be joined to issues through canonical ledger IDs, with compatibility fields intact and backfill coverage measured. That gives the graph and UI a reliable data source without depending on git-bug short-ID joins.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codex (GPT-5) \u003ccodex@openai.com\u003e","files":null}]}